flex-direction is a flexbox property which is used to define the direction in which we want to arrange the items.
It can be row (horizontal) or column (vertical). 
The direction defined by flex-direction becomes the main axis of flex-container(container on which flexbox is applied). 
The direction perpendicular to the main axis becomes the Cross-axis of the flex-container.

The flex-wrap property of flexbox makes the items move to the next line if the space in the current line is less. 
This makes the layout responsive as it adjusts upon the change in screen size. 
By default this property is set to 'nowrap', means that items won't wrap to next line upon decreased screen space.

Both these properties can be combined in a single on which is called as flex-flow. Using this property we can set both 
flex-direction and flex-wrap in one go.
